        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "The school notice"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "The school wanted to tell students about a sports day.\n\"A notice must give the facts in few words,\" said the teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "notice",
          "subject line",
          "formal"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A notice has a heading, the date, a short message with what, when and where, and the writer's name and post. It uses few words.\nA formal letter has the sender address, date, receiver address, subject line, a polite greeting such as Sir or Madam, the body, and closing like Yours faithfully with the signature.\nUse polite, correct and brief language in formal writing."
        }
      },
